# Flux UI LLM UI Development Instructions (2025)

_Last updated: October 2025_

- Always use the fetch tool to look up the latest component usage, installation commands, and best practices directly from the official Flux UI documentation: https://fluxui.dev/docs and https://fluxui.dev/components
- Do not rely on what you think you know about Flux UI components, as they are actively developed and frequently updated.
- For any Flux UI component, CLI command, or usage pattern, fetch the relevant page from the docs and follow the instructions there.

**Core Principles:**
- Flux UI components are open-source and designed for direct customization—review and extend them as needed for your project.
- Use the CLI (`pnpm dlx fluxui@latest add <component>`) to add or update components, or follow the install instructions in the documentation.
- Always import from the local `@/components/ui/<component>` path, as recommended in the docs.
- Follow accessibility and composition guidelines as described in https://fluxui.dev/docs and each component’s documentation.

**Summary:**
> For all Flux UI development, always use the fetch tool to look up the latest component documentation and usage from https://fluxui.dev/docs and https://fluxui.dev/components. Do not rely on static instructions or prior knowledge.